  m_Name: SteelPier
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  materialId: SteelPier
  displayName: Steel Pier
  introductionDescription: A braced steel tower that supports the bridge from
    below. Connect it between a solid foundation and a bridge joint to carry heavy
    loads down to the ground.
  introductionImage: {fileID: 0}
  almanacDescription: The Steel Pier uses a braced frame to carry vertical load
    in compression. It costs more per metre than the Concrete Pier and adds less
    weight to the bridge. A taller pier can buckle more easily, so use a sound
    foundation and brace the bridge where loads enter the pier.
  almanacImage: {fileID: 0}
